{"name":"Ormpe","status":"ok","title":"Ormpe","pageId":131822,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside role=\"region\" class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\">\n\n\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Ormpe</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography<sup id=\"cite_ref-TSS-62_2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TSS-62-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"alt spelling\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Alt. spelling</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Ompré, Ompre<sup id=\"cite_ref-NN_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-NN-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>note 1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">City</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"size\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Size</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Large</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Society<sup id=\"cite_ref-TSS-62_2-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TSS-62-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"races\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Races</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Human\" title=\"Human\">Humans</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Dwarves\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Dwarves\">dwarves</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Gnome\" title=\"Gnome\">gnomes</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Halfling\" title=\"Halfling\">halflings</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Commerce<sup id=\"cite_ref-TSS-62_2-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TSS-62-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"exports\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Exports</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Curna_emerald\" title=\"Curna emerald\">Curna emeralds</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Politics<sup id=\"cite_ref-TSS-62_2-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TSS-62-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"government\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Merchant Council</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">History<sup id=\"cite_ref-SS-123_3-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SS-123-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"population1\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Population</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">20000<sup id=\"cite_ref-TSS-62_2-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TSS-62-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1367_DR\" title=\"1367 DR\">1367&#160;DR</a><br>4500<sup id=\"cite_ref-SS-123_3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SS-123-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1373_DR\" title=\"1373 DR\">1373&#160;DR</a><br>0<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCG_4-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1479_DR\" title=\"1479 DR\">1479&#160;DR</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"ruler1\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Ruler</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Beholder\" title=\"Beholder\">Beholders</a>&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/147_DR\" title=\"147 DR\">147&#160;DR</a><br>A <a href=\"/wiki/Ghour\" title=\"Ghour\">ghour</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Demon\" title=\"Demon\">demon</a>&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/152_DR\" title=\"152 DR\">152&#160;DR</a><br>Merchant Council&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1103_DR\" title=\"1103 DR\">1103&#160;DR</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><span class=\"new\" title=\"Category:Inhabitants of Ormpe (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQ2F0ZWdvcnk6SW5oYWJpdGFudHNfb2ZfT3JtcGU/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Inhabitants of  Ormpe</span></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Locations_in_Ormpe\" title=\"Category:Locations in Ormpe\">Locations in  Ormpe</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><span class=\"new\" title=\"Category:Organizations in Ormpe (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQ2F0ZWdvcnk6T3JnYW5pemF0aW9uc19pbl9Pcm1wZT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Organizations in  Ormpe</span></nav>\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Ormpé</b><sup id=\"cite_ref-NN_1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-NN-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>note 1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> was a city along the coast of the <a href=\"/wiki/Golden_Water\" title=\"Golden Water\">Golden Water</a>. It was the fastest growing city in the region during the late 14<sup>th</sup> century DR.<sup id=\"cite_ref-TSS-62_2-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TSS-62-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Description\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Description</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Geography\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Geography</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Trade\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Trade</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Inhabitants\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Inhabitants</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Notes\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notes</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Appearances\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appearances</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Description\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ormpe?veaction=edit&section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Description\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <a href=\"/wiki/1373_DR\" title=\"1373 DR\">1373&#160;DR</a>, Ormpé was a rustic mining community.<sup id=\"cite_ref-SS-123_3-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SS-123-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Geography\">Geography</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Geography\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ormpe?veaction=edit&section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Geography\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Of all the cities in the Shining Lands, only Ormpé had large slum areas. The largest of them, the Quarter of No Hope, resided outside the walls.<sup id=\"cite_ref-TSS-62_2-6\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TSS-62-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trade\">Trade</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Trade\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ormpe?veaction=edit&section=3\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Trade\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <span class=\"new\" title=\"Gemstone chaka (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvR2Vtc3RvbmVfY2hha2E/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">gemstone chaka</span> was native to Ormpé.<sup id=\"cite_ref-TSS-56_5-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TSS-56-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Gnomes were a common sight in the city.<sup id=\"cite_ref-TSS-57_6-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TSS-57-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> So was the <span class=\"new\" title=\"Finglefall (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRmluZ2xlZmFsbD9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Finglefall</span> chaka.<sup id=\"cite_ref-TSS-S_7-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TSS-S-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The field glass was an invention of the gnomes of the city.<sup id=\"cite_ref-TSS-60_8-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TSS-60-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Most of the people in the Quarter of No Hope were migrant grain workers, though some tried to obtain mining jobs, which paid better. However, the Gemstone chaka preferred to hire dwarven miners and gnomish gemcutters, having come to an agreement with the Finglefall chaka: whoever wanted to work on the famous Curna emeralds needed to come to an agreement with at least one of those chakas.<sup id=\"cite_ref-TSS-62_2-7\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TSS-62-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> However, several chakas had made their fortunes with the sale of gemstones by <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372&#160;DR</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-SS-123_3-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SS-123-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>A lot of scholars lodged at the city on the way to use the Library of Curna.<sup id=\"cite_ref-TSS-66_9-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TSS-66-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: History\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ormpe?veaction=edit&section=4\" aria-label=\"Edit section: History\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ormpé was another fishing village that grew into a trade hub<sup id=\"cite_ref-SS-123_3-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SS-123-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> before it was conquered by <a href=\"/wiki/Beholder\" title=\"Beholder\">beholder</a> princes in the <a href=\"/wiki/147_DR\" title=\"147 DR\">Year of the Iron Colossus, 147 DR</a>. These beholders were defeated by <a href=\"/wiki/Demons\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Demons\">demons</a> come from the <a href=\"/wiki/Curna_Mountains\" title=\"Curna Mountains\">Curna Mountains</a> in the <a href=\"/wiki/153_DR\" title=\"153 DR\">Year of the Wolfstone, 153 DR</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-SS-117_10-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SS-117-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The leader of the demons was a nasty <span class=\"new\" title=\"Ghour demon (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvR2hvdXJfZGVtb24/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">ghour demon</span>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-SS-123_3-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SS-123-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The city was not recovered until the <a href=\"/wiki/1103_DR\" title=\"1103 DR\">Year of the Consuming Glory, 1103 DR</a>,<sup id=\"cite_ref-SS-118_11-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SS-118-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> when the forces of <a href=\"/wiki/Var\" title=\"Var\">Var</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Durpar\" title=\"Durpar\">Durpar</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Estagund\" title=\"Estagund\">Estagund</a> defeated the demons and forced their leader into flight; it was rumoured he took up with the local <a href=\"/wiki/Hill_giant\" title=\"Hill giant\">hill giants</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-SS-123_3-6\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SS-123-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>An influx of people started around <a href=\"/wiki/1365_DR\" title=\"1365 DR\">1365&#160;DR</a>, doubling the population by <a href=\"/wiki/1367_DR\" title=\"1367 DR\">1367&#160;DR</a>. The influx of people had gone well beyond even what the local ruling council expected: Ormpé developed a rather large slum.<sup id=\"cite_ref-TSS-62_2-8\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TSS-62-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> By <a href=\"/wiki/1373_DR\" title=\"1373 DR\">1373&#160;DR</a>, it was expected things would turn ugly if the squalor was left unaddressed.<sup id=\"cite_ref-SS-123_3-7\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SS-123-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Ormpé had fallen into the <a href=\"/wiki/Golden_Water\" title=\"Golden Water\">Golden Water</a> by <a href=\"/wiki/1479_DR\" title=\"1479 DR\">1479&#160;DR</a> DR.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCG_4-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Inhabitants\">Inhabitants</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Inhabitants\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ormpe?veaction=edit&section=5\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Inhabitants\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Though the city had started as merely the location for ironworks, the population doubled between 1365 and 1367; 5000 of them lived in slums by the later date. Ormpè had a large population of demihumans, particularly dwarves and gnomes, with many halflings as well, by that year.<sup id=\"cite_ref-TSS-62_2-9\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TSS-62-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Albeit the city continued to grow, it had only 4500 inhabitants in <a href=\"/wiki/1373_DR\" title=\"1373 DR\">1373&#160;DR</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-SS-123_3-8\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SS-123-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ormpe?veaction=edit&section=6\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\">Notes</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Notes\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ormpe?veaction=edit&section=7\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Notes\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<small><div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-NN-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-NN_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-NN_1-1\">1.1</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">The spelling of Ompré appears in <i>Shining South</i> page 123, and is repeated only in <i>Darkvision</i>, where Ompre is referred to only once. However, it is referred to as the sister city of Assur and Vaelan in both appearances. Given the similar context, it is assumed that the Ompre in <i>Darkvision</i> is the same as the one in <i>Shining South</i>, and the one in Shining South appears to be a misspelling of Ormpé, as it is employed as if the city had been referred to previously, and shares all the same letters, down to the accent on the last \"e\". Thus, this article is written following the conclusion that Ompré and Ormpé refer to the same city, perhaps because of a typo. The prevalent spelling is used again in <i>Forgotten Realms Campaign Guide</i>, the latest source, and thus Ormpé is preferred as the spelling in this article.</span>\n</li>\n</ol></div></small>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appearances\">Appearances</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Appearances\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ormpe?veaction=edit&section=8\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Appearances\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><dl><dt>Novels</dt>\n<dd><b><small>Referenced only</small></b></dd>\n<dd><i><a href=\"/wiki/Darkvision_(novel)\" title=\"Darkvision (novel)\">Darkvision</a></i></dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Ormpe?veaction=edit&section=9\" aria-label=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-TSS-62-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TSS-62_2-0\">1.00</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TSS-62_2-1\">1.01</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TSS-62_2-2\">1.02</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TSS-62_2-3\">1.03</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TSS-62_2-4\">1.04</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TSS-62_2-5\">1.05</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TSS-62_2-6\">1.06</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TSS-62_2-7\">1.07</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TSS-62_2-8\">1.08</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TSS-62_2-9\">1.09</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Tom_Prusa\" title=\"Tom Prusa\">Tom Prusa</a>&#160;(1993). <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Shining_South_(1993)\" title=\"The Shining South (1993)\">The Shining South</a></i>